  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_5a4bf16e96544a768aec8293ab22abdd",
      "statement": "Every platform service is a cell of a runtime-supplied reserved class: __D1Database, __Workflow, __KvNamespace, and __Queue (with script-scoped __Workflow.<script>), and user configs naming these classes are refused at deploy because the harness registers them in every isolate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/deploy.rs#L64-L81",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b33431cee0eba4e3ec9188f7430bde10a28b2b7f90abe9bf7fa0454744ec843e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_399e08691c784d6692ba0170c8f30f9b",
      "statement": "The unauthenticated /do/ route refuses every reserved scope through the single is_reserved_scope predicate, and /runtime/<SCOPE> is the only HMAC-authenticated entrance for reserved classes, so a newly added reserved class inherits both the refusal and the entrance with no new code.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/deploy.rs#L144-L161",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42d85791ec2a9364e35ee56bb6ca00fb7cf9aaa2939c8f9733ef4df0be5f0d7e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L2658-L2712",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3c48f6fdcef3c40fa7dc3e3e8c52d71adcaa75691c03c0908f0eb0f847b6f585:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8e0b616f999d4fe6b93cdfba75d287b3",
      "statement": "Class-name punctuation is a collision constraint (dots are illegal in JS class names but legal in cell scopes), and sharedness is per class: D1, KV, and Queue cells are fleet-wide so multiple Workers can bind one resource, while workflow cells are script-scoped, which is why workflow classes carry the script name.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/deploy.rs#L92-L128",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e7f8dc07a38330c1b2562d932923b1b491ce8fb5975bc43ef40cd072472faf2e:"
        },
        {
